Potential TypeScript issue: `matches(entry: (typeof searchEntries)[number], ...)` union; `entry.keywords` exists on both; fine. `Link to={entry.path}` where entry narrowed by filter callback? TypeScript doesn't narrow array filter result type unless type predicate. `pageHits` type remains `SearchEntry[]`, and `entry.path` union includes product path string; `Link to` might error. We can explicitly type the filter with predicate:
```ts
const pageHits = searchEntries.filter((entry): entry is PageSearchEntry => entry.group === "Halaman" && matches(...));
```
But PageSearchEntry isn't exported. Export types or use `Extract<SearchEntry, {group:"Halaman"}>`. In component:
```ts
import { searchEntries, type SearchEntry } from "@/data/search";
type PageEntry = Extract<SearchEntry, { group: "Halaman" }>;
type ProductEntry = Extract<SearchEntry, { group: "Produk" }>;
const pageHits = useMemo(
 () => searchEntries.filter((entry): entry is PageEntry => entry.group === "Halaman" && matches(entry,q)),
 [q]
);
```
Similarly product. This also narrows `entry.slug`. Without this, `productHits.map` entry.slug may error. Fix SearchDialog imports and filters.

Also `matches` parameter type can be `SearchEntry`.

Apply.

